WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.680
Welcome to Grade 1 English, Unit 7: Let's Go!.

2
00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:08.940
In this unit, your child learns how we travel and get around.

3
00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:16.520
They meet the words for ways to travel (walk, bus, car,
bicycle, boat) and learn to say how they go to school.

4
00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:23.160
They talk about journeys — going somewhere with the
people they love, staying safe, and enjoying the trip.

5
00:00:23.860 --> 00:00:29.800
The goal is warm, confident English about the
everyday world of going places — not perfect spelling.

6
00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:35.640
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

7
00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:43.700
By the end of this unit, you will be able to name common
ways to travel (walk, bus, car, bicycle, boat, train, plane).

8
00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:48.340
you will also say how they get to
school: “i go to school by ___.”.

9
00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:55.120
you will also say the action words for
travel (drive, ride, fly, float, walk).

10
00:00:55.930 --> 00:00:57.980
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

11
00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:04.680
Your vocabulary work begins with these
words: walk, bus, car, bicycle, boat, train.

12
00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:09.880
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

13
00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:13.360
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

14
00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:18.500
The reading sequence includes Amal's
Big Bus Ride and Talk about Let's Go!.

15
00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:20.320
Read actively.

16
00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:24.700
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

17
00:01:25.180 --> 00:01:28.700
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

18
00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:32.730
The first language focus is Language pattern 1.

19
00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:38.000
Listen to the model, point to the matching
picture, then say the pattern: I go by ___.

20
00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:45.180
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

21
00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:50.160
In speaking, you will complete Speaking 1 - Listen and point.

22
00:01:50.850 --> 00:01:55.640
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

23
00:01:56.720 --> 00:02:00.080
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

24
00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:03.780
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

25
00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:05.640
You are ready to begin.

26
00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:11.640
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

27
00:02:12.140 --> 00:02:14.340
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

28
00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:20.200
Use AI English for hints and feedback, and
bring your questions to the live sessions.
